.TH SQUARECROP 1 "October 2026" "squarecrop 2.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
squarecrop \- cut square JPEGs out of images, or pad them to a square
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B squarecrop.py
.RI [ switches ]
.RI [ files " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B squarecrop
produces square JPEG images from rectangular source images, either by cropping
a square of the shorter side or by padding the shorter side with a colour.
Supported inputs are jpg, jpeg, png, bmp, gif, tif, tiff and webp.
Output is always JPEG, named
.IR name _square_ mode .jpg ,
and existing files are never overwritten unless
.B \-w
is given; a numeric suffix (_001, _002, ...) is added instead.
.PP
Switches are case-insensitive:
.BR \-LS ,
.B \-ls
and
.B \-\-LeftSide
are identical.
.B \-\-switch=value
is accepted for long switches.
Wildcards in file arguments are expanded by the program itself.
.SH CROP MODES
The crop is a square whose side is the shorter dimension of the source.
Several modes may be given; one file per mode is written.
If none is given,
.B \-t
is assumed.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-top
Crop from the top (portrait images); centred on landscape images.
.TP
.BR \-ls ", " \-\-leftside ", " \-\-left
Crop from the left side (landscape images); centred on portrait images.
.TP
.BR \-rs ", " \-\-rightside ", " \-\-right
Crop from the right side (landscape images); centred on portrait images.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bottom
Crop from the bottom (portrait images); centred on landscape images.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-middle
Crop a square from the centre of the image.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pad ", " \-e ", " \-\-expand " \fICOLOR\fR"
Do not crop. Instead pad the shorter dimension to make a square.
.I COLOR
is
.BR black ,
.BR white ,
.B b
or
.BR w ,
or an RGB value written
.B 0xAABBCC
or
.BR #AABBCC .
A 100x200 image padded with black becomes 200x200 with 50 pixel black bars.
Cannot be combined with crop modes.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-resize " \fIN\fR"
Resize the result to N x N pixels.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIN\fR"
JPEG quality, 1\-100 (default 95).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIDIR\fR"
Write results to DIR, creating it if needed (default: next to the source).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing output files.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-strip\-metadata ", " \-\-nometadata
Do not copy EXIF and ICC profile data.
.SH INPUT SELECTION
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-current
Process all images in the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Process images in the current directory and all subdirectories.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file\-pattern ", " \-\-pattern " \fIGLOB\fR"
Only process files matching GLOB.
.PP
Files previously produced by squarecrop (\fI*_square_*.jpg\fR) are skipped
by these options. Images that are already square are skipped unless
.B \-z
requests a different size. Symbolic links are ignored.
.SH MISCELLANEOUS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Number of worker threads (default 4).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run ", " \-\-dryrun
Print the files that would be written; write nothing.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log
Log to squarecrop.log in the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each source and result as it is processed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error (no input, or conflicting switches).
.TP
.B 2
No matching files, or an invalid argument.
.TP
.B 3
One or more files failed; the rest were still processed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
squarecrop.py photo.jpg
squarecrop.py \-ls \-rs \-c
squarecrop.py \-i \-z 512 *.png
squarecrop.py \-\-pad 0x336699 \-r \-o out
squarecrop.py \-r \-f "*.png" \-q 90 \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3 and the Pillow library.
